# mightex_autosave.req
#
# Top-level autosave request file. Includes mightexChannel.req once per
# channel with different P=/R= macros -- this is the standard mitigation
# for autosave's known create_monitor_set() filename-collision behavior
# when the same request file name is loaded many times for different
# instances (documented from prior SR570 bring-up experience).
#
# Load THIS file once via set_pass0_restoreFile/set_pass1_restoreFile in
# st.cmd -- do not call those functions per-channel.
#
# STARTING WITH 3 CHANNELS FOR INITIAL TESTING. Extend to all 16 (same
# "file mightexChannel.req {...}" pattern, CHL 4-16) only after
# confirming autosave saves and restores correctly for these three,
# given the collision risk noted above -- same cautious rollout used for
# every other part of this IOC's bring-up.

file mightexChannel.req {"P=BL:LED:","R=Ch1:"}
file mightexChannel.req {"P=BL:LED:","R=Ch2:"}
file mightexChannel.req {"P=BL:LED:","R=Ch3:"}
